1. [AP01 high] sub/run.sh:1
   Problem: Agent runs with all permission checks turned off (--yolo)
   Why: Every tool call, including shell commands and file deletes, runs without approval. One prompt injection in a file, issue or web page the agent reads can run any command as you.
   Suggested change: Remove the bypass. Allow specific tools instead, and run unattended agents in a throwaway sandbox with no secrets and no network beyond what the task needs.

How to fix AP01 (Agent runs with all permission checks turned off):
   Example before:
      claude --dangerously-skip-permissions -p "fix the tests"
      "defaultMode": "bypassPermissions"
   Example after:
      claude -p "fix the tests" --allowedTools "Bash(npm test)" "Edit"
      "defaultMode": "default"
   Hardened policy template (for administrators): templates/policy/README.md

